2. How a draw is made: two draws of the nine spreads, made here with numpy (seed 2026)
   draw 1, largest value of each spread: inductance +0.0945 3.15 sd (pair 49); diode current +0.1127 2.25 sd (pair 19); difference inside a pair -0.0492 -2.46 sd (pair 33); pump phase (rad of pump phase) -0.6540 -3.75 sd (pair 29); pump level +0.2538 2.54 sd (pair 28); link strength +0.2961 2.96 sd (link 32); clock timing (periods) -0.0580 -2.90 sd (pair 6); supply level +0.0296 2.96 sd (pair 43); damping resistor -0.1158 -2.32 sd (pair 28)
   draw 2, largest value of each spread: inductance +0.0971 3.24 sd (pair 19); diode current +0.1484 2.97 sd (pair 15); difference inside a pair +0.0470 2.35 sd (pair 15); pump phase (rad of pump phase) -0.5046 -2.89 sd (pair 0); pump level -0.2860 -2.86 sd (pair 39); link strength -0.2318 -2.32 sd (link 61); clock timing (periods) -0.0490 -2.45 sd (pair 10); supply level +0.0244 2.44 sd (pair 44); damping resistor -0.1295 -2.59 sd (pair 16)
   Each value is the rms value of the spread times a standard normal number; it is not bounded. A run without noise or spread has none.

